.TH "RECORD\-EDIT\.SH" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-edit\.sh\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-edit\.sh\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-edit\.sh\fR opens the current or most recent output of \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR in \fBvi\fR for inspection or editing\. It sources \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR and uses the PID file and process state to determine which file to open:
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBIf \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is running\fR (the PID file exists and \fB/proc/<pid>\fR is present), the script resolves the program's current standard error file descriptor via \fBget_stderr\fR and opens it in \fBvi\fR\. This allows live inspection of a running workflow's stderr output\.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBIf \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is not running\fR (the PID file is absent or the process is no longer alive), the script opens the most recent output file matching the glob \fB$RECORD_START_PROGRAM\.????\-??\-??\.out\fR in \fBvi\fR\. A message is written to standard error noting that the program is not running\.
.IP "" 0
.SH "OPTIONS"
This script accepts no options or arguments\. All configuration is supplied via environment variables inherited from \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 if the program is running and \fBvi\fR exits successfully\.
.P
Returns \-1 (typically 255) if:
.IP "\(bu" 4
the PID file does not exist; or
.IP "\(bu" 4
the process is no longer running\.
.IP "" 0
.P
Note that in both failure cases \fBvi\fR is still launched before the script exits, so the exit status reflects the state \fIafter\fR \fBvi\fR closes\.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR
The name of the workflow program being monitored\. Used to locate the PID file and to glob for output files\. Set and validated by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR at source time\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR
Used by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR to construct the PID file path\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_PID_FILE\fR
Path to the PID file, exported by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR as \fB/tmp/record\.$USER\.$RECORD_DBTYPE\.$RECORD_START_PROGRAM\.pid\fR\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Open the stderr of a currently running workflow:
.IP "" 4
.nf
export RECORD_START_PROGRAM=my_sim
export RECORD_DBTYPE=sqlite3
record\-edit\.sh
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Open the most recent output file of a completed workflow:
.IP "" 4
.nf
export RECORD_START_PROGRAM=my_sim
export RECORD_DBTYPE=sqlite3
record\-edit\.sh
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR
Common library sourced at startup\. Must be present in the working directory or on \fBPATH\fR\.
.TP
\fB/tmp/record\.<USER>\.<RECORD_DBTYPE>\.<RECORD_START_PROGRAM>\.pid\fR
PID file written by the workflow run\. Read to determine whether \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is currently running\.
.TP
\fB$RECORD_START_PROGRAM\.????\-??\-??\.out\fR
Glob pattern used to find output files when the program is not running\. Matched in the current working directory\.
